  "step_3": "The decision reason emphasizes losses and prefers the lottery with the more favorable (less severe) maximum loss. However, in this case, both lotteries have the same maximum loss (0 Euros), so the reason would not favor one over the other. The individual, however, does not discuss losses at all. Instead, they focus on the slightly higher probability of winning in one lottery, which reflects a gain-oriented, rather than loss-averse, reasoning. The information considered by the individual (probability of winning) does not align with the information emphasized by the decision reason (maximum loss). Furthermore, the justification (favoring a higher chance to win) is based on gains, whereas the decision reason treats losses as more important. Therefore, there is no evidence that the individual applied the loss-based decision reason. The reasoning in the report contradicts the core principle of the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
